		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Updated Voice prompts  2024/03/18]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3883&amp;p=30321#p30321"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>The voice prompt files have been updated to include entries for new or revised functionality e.g. DMR Force DMO<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest/" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest/</a><br><br>Note.<br><br>Although the firmware now has Romanian language as an option we don't have voice prompt texts for that language</div></blockquote>Dear Colleagues.<br>Thank you for your work and, above all, your time.<br>However, I must say that your recent activities have been a total disaster.<br>I mean the Polish language, which has been totally converted and the messages have been used from some electronic translator.<br>There was already a thread in December last year together with my colleague sp7czo we sent manually translated files for Polish.<br>I daresay that, apart from English, it was one of the best translations for niche languages like Polish.<br>What is now available for download is absolutely and completely unusable.<br>Wouldn't it be possible to restore for our language the older version of the files, the ones we gave you?<br>What is currently there can simply be removed. It is better that there is no Polish language than it should look like this, especially since you have, after all, ready source files.<br>There is even a relevant thread on the forum.<br>I know that the key issue is that translations are needed for new features.<br>But it is better that a single message is not read than it is to be what it is now.<br>I would very much appreciate your taking a moment of your time on this issue.<br><br>73<br>Blind op Pawel sq9hht</div></blockquote>Wow, I guess you forgot a small detail, everyone here is doing that FOR FREE, on their spare time, so I strongly suggest you to have a little more respect for that. Take care about the words you're using.<br>You're warned.<br><br>Next, the current voice prompt file is 100% identical to the that SP7CZO sent me, and it has been validated by him (from his email):<blockquote class="uncited"><div>If you publish voice files in this version, I assure you that Polish users will be satisfied. I recommend myself for the future.</div></blockquote> <br><br>To prove it, here is the diff of the current (latest) version, and the one he sent me in December:<div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>--- /home/daniel/tmp/lang/polish/From_december/wordlist_polish.csv2024-03-23 03:58:32.766242015 +0100+++ languages/polish/wordlist_polish.csv2024-03-21 11:36:26.815478058 +0100@@ -359,3 +359,5 @@ aprs_turn_time,,,czas zwrotu auto_lock,,,automatyczna blokada +trackball,,,Trackball+dmr_force_dmo,,,DMR Force D M O</code></pre></div>So, if the resulting voice package is just crap in your eyes, I think you'd better to email Jeff Bezos to tell him how his (free) Amazon Polly service is crap. I think he will really appreciate that.<br><br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sat Mar 23, 2024 3:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
